# A 32-bit reference saves four bytes an object and is decoded at each read. In a layout that the program makes seldom every reference is a 64-bit one, and its cell grows for that. A hidden word stays as it is.
# The same program as widen-reference-into-padding.ir, where `testing=NoLayoutIsMadeSeldom` keeps the references narrow but for those that find free bytes in their cells
# FORM: AsRead
# OPTIONS: references=narrow only-passes=AnalyzeFlow
# RUN: plan-slots

# CHECK: L0 CompiledObject size=32
# CHECK-NEXT: "next" JSValue @16
# CHECK-NEXT: L1 CompiledObject size=32
# CHECK-NEXT: "node" Cell @16
# CHECK-NEXT: L2 CompiledObject size=32
# CHECK-NEXT: "label" Cell @16
# CHECK-NEXT: L3 CompiledObject size=32
# CHECK-NEXT: "title" JSValue @16
# CHECK-NEXT: L4 CompiledObject size=48
# CHECK-NEXT: "left" JSValue @16
# CHECK-NEXT: "right" JSValue @24
# CHECK-NEXT: "parent" JSValue @32
# CHECK-NEXT: "child" JSValue @40
# CHECK-NEXT: L5 CompiledObject size=32
# CHECK-NEXT: "link" JSValue @16
# CHECK-NEXT: extra Cell32 @24
# PROGRAM-OF: widen-reference-into-padding.ir
